.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH nexusctl 1  "nexusctl 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
nexusctl \- Command\-line client for nexusd
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnexusctl\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-terse\fR] [\fB\-\-pretty\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-separator\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-bus\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-polkit\-agent\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Command\-line client for nexusd
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format: human, terse, json, or pretty
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
terse
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
pretty
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for `\-\-format json`
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-terse\fR
Shorthand for `\-\-format terse` (separator\-joined, one record per line — ideal for shell scripts)
.TP
\fB\-\-pretty\fR
Shorthand for `\-\-format pretty` (verbose single\-record view)
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<FIELDS>\fR
Comma\-separated field whitelist for `\-\-terse` output
.TP
\fB\-\-separator\fR \fI<SEPARATOR>\fR [default: :]
Separator for `\-\-terse` output. Default `:`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to use ANSI colors
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI colors (equivalent to `\-\-color never`)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Override the D\-Bus call timeout for this invocation (seconds)
.TP
\fB\-\-bus\fR \fI<ADDRESS>\fR
D\-Bus bus address (for test harnesses running on session bus)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log D\-Bus calls and signal subscriptions to stderr
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-interactive\fR
Fail instead of prompting. Default: auto\-detect TTY
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-polkit\-agent\fR
Skip auto\-spawning `pkttyagent` for PolicyKit prompts. Useful when the caller has already got an agent, or explicitly wants mutating commands to fail hard on AuthFailed
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Alternative config file path
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
nexusctl\-status(1)
Show overall daemon status
.TP
nexusctl\-iface(1)
Interface operations
.TP
nexusctl\-eth(1)
Ethernet shortcuts (equivalent to `iface ... \-\-kind ethernet`)
.TP
nexusctl\-wifi(1)
Wi\-Fi operations
.TP
nexusctl\-bt(1)
Bluetooth operations
.TP
nexusctl\-gnss(1)
GNSS operations
.TP
nexusctl\-profile(1)
Profile management
.TP
nexusctl\-power(1)
PowerState control
.TP
nexusctl\-admin(1)
Administrative operations
.TP
nexusctl\-watch(1)
Subscribe to D\-Bus signals and print a live event stream
.TP
nexusctl\-completions(1)
Emit a shell completion script on stdout
.TP
nexusctl\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
